7.1 Team page: leadership and people
The /team page is where IData introduces its leadership and its people. Build it in three layers, all driven by src/content/team.ts:
1. Leadership: large featured cards for the CEO and other leaders (for example Founder and CEO, CTO, Head of Data and AI, Head of Delivery, Head of Business Development). Each card shows a big photo, name, title, a two-line bio, three focus areas and social links. Clicking a card opens a detail panel with the full bio and the services that person leads.
2. Core team: a grid of team cards grouped by service area (AI, Data, Software, Operations), with a filter chips row.
3. Extended network: vetted freelancers and partners in a smaller card style, with a short note on how IData vets and reviews freelance work. Switch this layer on or off with a config flag.
Each person entry in team.ts has: id, name, title, level (leadership, core, extended), area, photo, bio, focus (list), links (LinkedIn, GitHub, email), and order (to control display order). Adding a person is one new entry plus one photo in public/images/team/.
End the page with a Next step band (Work with us, Book a Call, Join the network). Also add a short Meet the leadership teaser with a Meet the team CTA on the About page, and keep the Home page unchanged so it stays short.
8. Home page specification
The home page must be short: about three screens on desktop, and every section must lead somewhere through a CTA. Build these sections in this order:
1. Hero: animated gradient mesh background using the theme colors, a short headline, one supporting line, two buttons (Request a Quote, Book a Call), and a small row of trust signals. Headline animates in word by word. A subtle floating dashboard or data-visual graphic reacts to the mouse.
2. Continuous marquee strip: an infinite horizontal ticker (often called a logo marquee or logo slider) showing tools and technologies IData works with and, later, client logos. Two rows moving in opposite directions, pausing on hover, edge fade, smooth with no jump at loop point. Items come from partners.ts.
3. Services: four interactive cards in a grid. Each card has an icon, one-line promise, three mini bullet points and an Explore CTA. Spotlight glow follows the cursor and the card tilts slightly in 3D.
4. Featured demo: one large video card (click to load the YouTube video) beside three short proof points with animated counters.
5. Reviews strip: an auto-scrolling carousel of three visible review cards with a Read all reviews CTA.
6. Final call to action band: large headline, Request a Quote and Book a Call.
7. Footer (Section 13).
Do not add more sections. Do not repeat content that exists on its own page; teaser plus CTA only.
