Required design qualities
• UUID primary keys, created_at and updated_at timestamps with an update trigger, foreign keys with sensible delete rules, check constraints for ratings and statuses, indexes on foreign keys, status and created_at.
• Row-level security on every table. Visitors can insert leads, pending reviews and newsletter signups, and can read approved reviews only. A client reads only their own projects, milestones, published deliverables and messages. Team members read projects they belong to. Only admins read leads and manage everything. Use a helper function is_admin().
• Storage buckets: attachments (private, lead uploads), deliverables (private, signed download links), review-photos (public), avatars (public). Limit file size and type.
• Provide seed.sql with sample rows for demo purposes only.
• Everything is reached through src/services/database.ts, so replacing Supabase later means rewriting that one file and moving the SQL.
15. Forms and email
• Every form (quote, review, newsletter, contact) saves to the database first, so nothing is lost if email fails.
• After saving, the front end calls api/notify.ts, a Vercel serverless function that emails the owner through Resend (free tier) using environment variables OWNER_EMAIL, RESEND_API_KEY and FROM_EMAIL. If these are empty, skip the email silently and rely on the admin area.
• The quote form fields: name, email, company, service of interest, budget range, project description, optional file (limit 5 MB), consent checkbox.
• Spam protection: hidden honeypot field, minimum fill time, basic rate limit in the function, and optional Cloudflare Turnstile behind a feature flag.
• Show a success state with Next step cards (Book a Call, See case studies), and an error state with a mailto fallback.
16. Booking
Use a Calendly inline embed, loaded only on /contact and in a modal from Book a Call buttons. The link is the single value calendlyUrl in site.config.ts. If it is empty, show a fallback card with the owner's email instead. Calendly has a free plan with limits (the owner should confirm what it includes today). Keep the booking code behind src/services/booking.ts so Cal.com or another tool can replace it.
17. Video and media
• Use at most three videos in total, defined in src/content/videos.ts (YouTube ID, title, poster image).
• Use a click-to-load cover image, then load the privacy-friendly YouTube embed. Videos never autoplay with sound and never load before the user clicks.
• No self-hosted video files. Images in WebP or AVIF, responsive sizes, lazy loading, explicit width and height to avoid layout jumps. Keep each image under about 200 KB.
• The hero and card visuals use CSS, SVG and canvas effects, not large media files.
18. Search
Build a client-side search index from services, case studies, team and FAQs using Fuse.js. Show it in the command palette with grouped results, keyboard navigation and recent searches. No server calls.
