The agent must produce both files, in plain, friendly language for a non-expert owner, with exact file paths, exact variable names and copy-paste commands.
20.1 README.md (public, for visitors and collaborators)
• What IData is and who it serves, in a short intro with a screenshot placeholder.
• The full site structure: a page tree with every route, what each page is for, and how the pages link to each other.
• What a visitor can do: explore services, watch a demo, read reviews, request a quote, book a call, sign in to the portal.
• A short feature list and an architecture overview diagram in text.
• How to contact IData. No setup steps and no secrets in this file; point to OWNER_GUIDE.md for those.
20.2 OWNER_GUIDE.md (private setup guide for Isaac)
Include these sections in this order:
1. Quick start: install Node.js, run npm install and npm run dev, see the site in demo mode.
2. Everything you must provide (master checklist table): item, where to enter it, exact file or variable name, required or optional. Cover: logo files, favicon, social share image, brand name and tagline, theme accent colors, owner email, social links, Calendly link, service descriptions, case studies, team members, reviews, videos, FAQs, legal text, Supabase keys, email keys.
3. Logo and images: exact folders and file names (public/brand/logo.svg, logo-mark.svg, favicon.ico, og-image.png at 1200 by 630), recommended sizes for team photos, case study covers and review avatars, and format and weight limits.
4. Editing content: for every file in src/content, an annotated example showing each field and what it controls.
5. Environment variables: a table of every variable in .env.example, what it is, and where to find it in the Supabase, Resend and Vercel dashboards.
6. Supabase setup, step by step: create the project, run schema.sql, policies.sql and optional seed.sql, create storage buckets, configure sign-in and redirect URLs, make yourself the first admin with a provided SQL snippet, and test a form submission.
7. Email setup: create a Resend account, verify the sender, copy the key, set the variables.
8. Calendly setup: create an event type, copy the link into site.config.ts.
