21. Build order and acceptance criteria
Build order: (1) project setup, config, design tokens, layout, header, menu, footer; (2) home page and shared components; (3) services, work, team, about; (4) reviews page; (5) contact, forms, booking; (6) Supabase schema, auth and portal; (7) admin area; (8) search; (9) polish, performance, accessibility; (10) both documentation files.
Acceptance criteria
• Every route in Section 7 loads and works on a 360-pixel phone.
• The header has no more than three plain links plus Menu, Search and Request a Quote.
• The home page is about three screens long and contains only the sections in Section 8.
• The marquee runs continuously without a visible jump and pauses on hover.
• The project runs with no environment variables set (demo mode) and with them set (live mode).
• A quote request is saved and the owner is emailed when email keys exist.
• A pending review appears only after admin approval.
• A client sees only their own project; a visitor cannot read leads.
• No more than three videos, none loading before a click.
• Both documentation files exist and every owner input is listed with its exact location.
• When finished, the agent prints a short summary: files created, what the owner must provide next, and how to run the project.
